  <content>
    <section>
      <para dir="ltr">
        <figure>
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_02_07_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <para dir="ltr">The figure shows the graph of the equation used to convert temperature in Celsius to temperature in Fahrenheit: \(F = 9/5 C + 32\).</para>
      <para dir="ltr">\(F = 9/5C + 32\) is used to convert temperatures, \(C\), on the Celsius scale to temperatures, \(F\), on the Fahrenheit scale. Identify and interpret the slope and \(F\)-intercept.</para>
    </section>
  </content>
